nio: retarget PID1 boost onto the exec'd thread (it was boosting a dead thread)

Run 700 proved the exec tail fully succeeds: D11 self_kill=1, D12/D13
(terminate old_task) pass, C05/C06 (FINAL_WAIT wake) pass, E06 ret=0.
No UB01/IPROBE follows; last line is SEL ... p1pri=1f. task_terminate_internal
killed the old PID1 thread, but nio_pid1_thread still points at that dead
thread, so thread_setrun()'s boost never touches the new exec thread --
it wakes at default 31 and starves behind kernel threads (the run-690 bug,
now with a different thread). Only retarget the global here; the wake goes
through thread_setrun() where the proven boost lifts the new thread to 94.
E07 marks the retarget on the panel.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -1169,6 +1169,9 @@
 	int (*getc)(bool);
 };
 extern struct nio_wd_console_ops cons_ops[];
+/* nio: exec retargets the PID1 boost/diagnostic thread onto the new exec
+ * thread; defined in osfmk/kern/sched_prim.c. */
+extern thread_t nio_pid1_thread;
 
 static void
 nio_emark(const char *s)
@@ -5339,6 +5342,16 @@
 
 		/* Release the thread ref returned by cloneproc */
 		if (imgp->ip_new_thread) {
+			/* nio: old PID1 thread was terminated above (D11 self_kill=1, D13
+			 * passed in run 700), but nio_pid1_thread still points at that
+			 * dead thread -- so the thread_setrun() boost never reaches the
+			 * NEW exec thread, which wakes at default priority 31 and starves
+			 * behind 81/91 kernel threads (run 700 last line p1pri=1f).
+			 * Retarget the boost/diagnostic thread here: the wake below goes
+			 * through thread_setrun(), where the existing boost lifts it to 94. */
+			nio_pid1_thread = imgp->ip_new_thread;
+			nio_emark("\nnio: E07 retarget nthread=");
+			nio_ehex((unsigned)(unsigned long)imgp->ip_new_thread);
 			/* wake up the new exec thread */
 			nio_emark("\nnio: C05 before FINAL_WAIT wake");
 			task_clear_return_wait(get_threadtask(imgp->ip_new_thread), TCRW_CLEAR_FINAL_WAIT);
